<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:18Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Syria: How  the 'house of sisters' threat split society</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56659e2e406b46a129225919221fdef238516c7cb332be89844076c8fb1e84c0</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/syria-how-the-house-of-sisters-threat-split-society/a-79192163--b9de2b546f7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/syria-how-the-house-of-sisters-threat-split-society/a-79192163?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rumor has it that the 'house of sisters' is where kidnapped women from other Syrian sects are forced to convert to Islam. Nobody knows if it really exists, but it's being used to create communal tensions anyway.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trafficked into fraud: An African crisis situation in Cambodia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63bbf3f442c98d4798bbfc631381f5583ad78932aa31b3e63004651db18f9651</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967--d423991a2cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cambodia's crackdown on scam operators is stranding young African trafficking victims in the Asian country with no money, no passport and no prospects.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Putin rejects mobilization rumors, many Russians unconvinced</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c0c754c2ba514f749d2275c52dda4ca25be102a3de9bb3d2ff0c6b9fe79a2a8</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T05:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/putin-rejects-mobilization-rumors-many-russians-unconvinced/a-79193386--b343555e2833.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/putin-rejects-mobilization-rumors-many-russians-unconvinced/a-79193386?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia’s President Vladimir Putin has dismissed rumors about military mobilization. But many Russians, including many DW users, say they are preparing for the possibility.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Dallas Republican convention: How Trump looms over midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d143b8e255a62b270b27ce0d32b1b24251132254b81e193c990e439f8f10e62</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T05:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dallas-republican-convention-how-trump-looms-over-midterms/a-79189744--12ee322d24e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dallas-republican-convention-how-trump-looms-over-midterms/a-79189744?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump is not on the ballot in the midterm elections — but the first Republican midterm convention is putting him center stage. It's a strategy that could prove risky for the party.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German economy frets about Saxony-Anhalt election results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8f6a8ae3d28f4e865b53016fc306c84641924cc6971a8d66debabf002439f67</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-economy-frets-about-saxony-anhalt-election-results/a-79162871--94d137604c23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-economy-frets-about-saxony-anhalt-election-results/a-79162871?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD won the election in the eastern German state by a wide margin. While politicians and election analysts are still debating the reasons for the far-right party's popularity, economists are sounding the alarm.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How Mao Zedong's legacy still shapes China 50 years on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30f481d6e5245a94db4eec53cbf85ac622ed1d36e5e2b7297d7e87aaff9821f3</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T14:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-mao-zedong-s-legacy-still-shapes-china-50-years-on/a-79189751--83b4fb70b8d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-mao-zedong-s-legacy-still-shapes-china-50-years-on/a-79189751?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China has transformed since Mao Zedong's death 50 years ago. But his legacy endures — from Xi Jinping's rule to a new wave of Mao nostalgia among young Chinese.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ratko Mladic’s funeral casts shadow over Bosnia and Herzegovina vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0aa7c796df2c10f901e4a0994a25764e4553314712cec144d528c37cb29987af</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T14:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ratko-mladic-s-funeral-casts-shadow-over-bosnia-and-herzegovina-vote/a-79189319--342fd5cbe6c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ratko-mladic-s-funeral-casts-shadow-over-bosnia-and-herzegovina-vote/a-79189319?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ratko Mladic’s funeral in Belgrade, attended by Serbian and Bosnian Serb leaders, has deepened regional tensions and could affect the upcoming election in Bosnia and Herzegovina.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Japan's empty temples seek new ways to survive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a9bc263b4e2a3ff905b0d794fd62a45b9fc724a8ef41386f83200851a0b1b7f</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-s-empty-temples-seek-new-ways-to-survive/a-79157964--7eea677a26bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-s-empty-temples-seek-new-ways-to-survive/a-79157964?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With a declining population, shrinking congregations and growing economic pressures, temples are struggling to stay relevant. As more temples are sold or closed, is religion in decline in modern Japan?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US-Canada tariff dispute weighs on cross-border ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c4ce66833f2a230d6112775a8fe034eedb9242b3c663b33860b84593a013c69</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T10:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-canada-tariff-dispute-weighs-on-cross-border-ties/a-78815803--082b25646c1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-canada-tariff-dispute-weighs-on-cross-border-ties/a-78815803?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Canada's retaliatory tariffs take effect, Canadian and US car industries fear the trade war will hit them hard, while Canadians are cutting back on travel.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya: Crackdown on foreign traders prompts xenophobia fears</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34aefad9a9b99f082d5b6d7bc4dda2590738726a9c65fb970776774054a1dc04</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-crackdown-on-foreign-traders-prompts-xenophobia-fears/a-79143847--a8e571d0a365.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-crackdown-on-foreign-traders-prompts-xenophobia-fears/a-79143847?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Concerns about xenophobia are rising in Kenya after President William Ruto ordered a crackdown on foreigners working as hawkers. The government insists however that legally documented foreign traders remain protected.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Morocco earthquake 3 years on: 'No one has remembered us'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cd5d0eb1d16dd6a61a0422bba2fbed8ac033d522d88f0d9092dcb5bdca62054</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T18:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/morocco-earthquake-3-years-on-no-one-has-remembered-us/a-78874844--cbd4f3eb032b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/morocco-earthquake-3-years-on-no-one-has-remembered-us/a-78874844?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Morocco has rebuilt thousands of homes since the 2023 earthquake. But some survivors are still living in tents and say they have received no state aid.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
